BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  A farmer from the First Village approached the fountain during a drought. Though her own crops) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (     thirmed, she poured in one precious bucket. It flowed across, becoming three buckets for th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    e Second Village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (  The people of the Second Village faced a choice. They could keep all three buckets, or honor t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    he farmer's trust. Their elder said, "Trust is the seed of abundance. Selfishness is the roo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    t of drought.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (  They returned two buckets through the fountain. The farmer now had two buckets-more than she b) Tj ET
