BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages were separated by a barren valley. Each village had a sacre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        d spring that produced five measures of water daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The Sky Spirits whispered to the villages: "What you pour into the valley shall flow to th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        e other side as a river three times as strong.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The First Village feared deception. "If we send our water," they said, "the other village ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        may keep it all." So they sent nothing, and both remained parched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      But then a wise elder spoke: "True prosperity flows in circles, not lines. Water sent forw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        ard must return backward, or the cycle dies.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      The First Village poured their five measures into the valley. It multiplied to fifteen, re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        aching the Second Village as an abundant river. The Second Village rejoiced, but the eld) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        er reminded them: "The gift must return, or tomorrow's springs run dry.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      The Second Village returned seven measures - not merely what was sent, but a fair share of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (         what was received. Both villages prospered.) Tj ET
