BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      A farmer from the First Village approached the fountain during a drought. Though her own c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        rops thirmed, she poured in one precious bucket. It flowed across, becoming three bucket) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        s for the Second Village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      The people of the Second Village faced a choice. They could keep all three buckets, or hon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        or the farmer's trust. Their elder said, "Trust is the seed of abundance. Selfishness is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         the root of drought.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      They returned two buckets through the fountain. The farmer now had two buckets-more than s) Tj ET
